{"module":"performance","voice":"male","duration":312.1,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Equal or better: what the evidence shows","start":0.0,"end":3.4,"words":[[0.05,0.57],[0.57,0.67],[0.67,1.19],[1.56,1.87],[1.87,2.08],[2.08,2.81],[2.81,3.22]]},{"el":"intro","text":"A common defense of today's gaps is that they reflect differences in effort or ability.","start":4.2,"end":8.86,"words":[[4.24,4.37],[4.37,4.69],[4.69,5.07],[5.07,5.2],[5.2,5.59],[5.59,5.84],[5.84,5.97],[5.97,6.16],[6.16,6.36],[6.36,6.8],[6.8,7.38],[7.38,7.51],[7.51,7.76],[7.76,7.83],[7.83,8.34]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Researchers have tested that directly, by sending out identical applications and changing only the name or race.","start":9.21,"end":16.92,"words":[[9.26,9.86],[9.86,10.08],[10.08,10.53],[10.53,10.75],[10.75,11.5],[11.76,11.99],[11.99,12.44],[12.44,12.66],[12.66,13.41],[13.41,14.24],[14.24,14.46],[14.46,15.13],[15.13,15.51],[15.51,15.66],[15.66,15.96],[15.96,16.03],[16.03,16.41]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This module shows what they found, and what Black Americans achieved while those barriers were in place.","start":17.27,"end":24.23,"words":[[17.32,17.56],[17.56,18.05],[18.05,18.38],[18.38,18.62],[18.62,18.86],[18.86,19.35],[19.64,19.88],[19.88,20.13],[20.13,20.45],[20.45,21.19],[21.19,21.68],[21.68,22.0],[22.0,22.33],[22.33,22.82],[22.82,22.98],[22.98,23.14],[23.14,23.63]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Same résumé, different callbacks","start":24.58,"end":27.73,"words":[[24.63,25.03],[25.03,25.83],[26.18,26.88],[26.88,27.58]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In a famous 2004 experiment, economists Marianne Bertrand and Sendhil Mullainathan answered job ads in Boston and Chicago with fake résumés.","start":28.43,"end":38.81,"words":[[28.48,28.63],[28.63,28.79],[28.79,29.25],[29.25,30.1],[30.1,31.03],[31.31,32.08],[32.08,32.54],[32.54,33.09],[33.09,33.32],[33.32,33.86],[33.86,34.64],[34.64,35.02],[35.02,35.33],[35.33,35.57],[35.57,35.72],[35.72,36.18],[36.18,36.42],[36.42,36.96],[36.96,37.19],[37.19,37.5],[37.5,38.2]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Identical résumés with white-sounding names (like Emily or Greg) got about 50% more callbacks than those with Black-sounding names (like Lakisha or Jamal).","start":39.16,"end":48.42,"words":[[39.2,39.88],[39.88,40.43],[40.43,40.64],[40.64,41.39],[41.39,41.73],[41.73,42.0],[42.0,42.35],[42.35,42.41],[42.41,42.69],[42.93,43.13],[43.13,43.48],[43.48,44.23],[44.23,44.36],[44.36,44.84],[44.84,45.05],[45.05,45.32],[45.32,45.53],[45.53,46.28],[46.28,46.62],[46.62,46.9],[46.9,47.31],[47.31,47.38],[47.38,47.86]]},{"el":"s0","text":"A white-sounding name was worth about as much as eight extra years of experience.","start":48.77,"end":54.57,"words":[[48.82,48.99],[48.99,49.9],[49.9,50.23],[50.23,50.48],[50.48,50.73],[50.73,51.14],[51.14,51.31],[51.31,51.64],[51.64,51.81],[51.81,52.05],[52.05,52.55],[52.55,52.88],[52.88,53.05],[53.05,54.13]]},{"el":"s0","text":"It wasn't a one-off.","start":54.92,"end":56.34,"words":[[54.97,55.08],[55.08,55.42],[55.42,55.54],[55.54,55.88]]},{"el":"s0","text":"A 2017 analysis of every field experiment of this kind since 1989 found that white applicants received on average about 36% more callbacks than equally qualified Black applicants, with no decline over 25 years.","start":56.69,"end":72.61,"words":[[56.73,56.88],[56.88,57.93],[57.93,58.53],[58.53,58.68],[58.68,58.98],[58.98,59.28],[59.28,60.1],[60.1,60.25],[60.25,60.47],[60.47,60.85],[60.85,61.15],[61.15,62.27],[62.27,62.64],[62.64,62.87],[62.87,63.16],[63.16,63.84],[63.84,64.29],[64.29,64.44],[64.44,64.88],[64.88,65.26],[65.26,66.3],[66.3,66.45],[66.45,66.98],[66.98,67.2],[67.2,67.65],[67.65,68.32],[68.32,68.62],[68.62,69.37],[69.63,69.86],[69.86,70.08],[70.08,70.6],[70.6,70.9],[70.9,71.65],[71.65,72.02]]},{"el":"s0","text":"A 2021–2022 study that sent about 83,000 applications to large U.S. companies found the same bias, concentrated in a minority of firms.","start":72.96,"end":83.53,"words":[[73.0,73.13],[73.13,75.16],[75.16,75.49],[75.49,75.69],[75.69,75.95],[75.95,76.28],[76.28,77.2],[77.2,77.92],[77.92,78.05],[78.05,78.31],[78.31,78.64],[78.97,79.49],[79.49,79.82],[79.82,79.95],[79.95,80.21],[80.21,80.61],[80.84,81.69],[81.69,81.82],[81.82,81.95],[81.95,82.54],[82.54,82.67],[82.67,83.0]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Sociologist Devah Pager went further in 2003: she sent real testers to apply for jobs in Milwaukee.","start":83.88,"end":91.18,"words":[[83.92,84.95],[84.95,85.25],[85.25,85.69],[85.69,85.99],[85.99,86.29],[86.29,86.43],[86.43,87.4],[87.66,87.81],[87.81,88.1],[88.1,88.4],[88.4,88.84],[88.84,88.99],[88.99,89.36],[89.36,89.51],[89.51,89.88],[89.88,90.03],[90.03,90.62]]},{"el":"s0","text":"White applicants who said they had a criminal record got called back about as often as Black applicants with no record.","start":91.53,"end":98.27,"words":[[91.58,91.86],[91.86,92.5],[92.5,92.64],[92.64,92.85],[92.85,93.06],[93.06,93.27],[93.27,93.41],[93.41,93.98],[93.98,94.33],[94.33,94.54],[94.54,94.83],[94.83,95.04],[95.04,95.39],[95.39,95.53],[95.53,95.82],[95.82,95.96],[95.96,96.24],[96.24,96.87],[96.87,97.09],[97.09,97.3],[97.3,97.72]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Twice as good, still behind","start":99.17,"end":102.24,"words":[[99.22,99.8],[99.8,100.02],[100.02,100.48],[100.88,101.34],[101.34,102.14]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Many Black parents tell their children they must be “twice as good to get half as much.”","start":102.94,"end":108.32,"words":[[103.01,103.31],[103.31,103.6],[103.6,104.2],[104.2,104.42],[104.42,104.64],[104.64,105.24],[105.24,105.46],[105.46,105.76],[105.76,105.91],[105.91,106.28],[106.28,106.43],[106.43,106.65],[106.65,106.8],[106.8,107.02],[107.02,107.25],[107.25,107.39],[107.39,107.77]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The data backs them up: at every level of education, Black workers have higher unemployment than white workers, and Black college graduates earn less than white college graduates.","start":108.67,"end":119.98,"words":[[108.71,108.87],[108.87,109.24],[109.24,109.55],[109.55,109.77],[109.77,110.0],[110.26,110.41],[110.41,110.72],[110.72,111.09],[111.09,111.25],[111.25,112.08],[112.34,112.64],[112.64,113.02],[113.02,113.25],[113.25,113.55],[113.55,114.46],[114.46,114.68],[114.68,114.99],[114.99,115.44],[115.7,115.93],[115.93,116.23],[116.23,116.69],[116.69,117.37],[117.37,117.52],[117.52,117.74],[117.74,117.97],[117.97,118.27],[118.27,118.73],[118.73,119.48]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The gaps persist even when researchers compare people with the same degree, the same field and the same experience.","start":120.33,"end":127.38,"words":[[120.38,120.53],[120.53,120.82],[120.82,121.26],[121.26,121.56],[121.56,121.78],[121.78,122.36],[122.36,122.8],[122.8,123.17],[123.17,123.39],[123.39,123.53],[123.53,123.83],[123.83,124.26],[124.52,124.67],[124.67,124.96],[124.96,125.25],[125.25,125.47],[125.47,125.62],[125.62,125.91],[125.91,126.86]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Education: the record and a popular claim","start":128.28,"end":131.37,"words":[[128.33,129.15],[129.41,129.56],[129.56,129.94],[129.94,130.16],[130.16,130.31],[130.31,130.83],[130.83,131.21]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Documented: Black women enroll in college at high rates, and Historically Black Colleges and Universities (HBCUs), about 3% of U.S. colleges, produce a large share of Black graduates, doctors, lawyers and engineers, according to UNCF.","start":132.07,"end":150.17,"words":[[132.12,133.05],[133.32,133.64],[133.64,134.02],[134.02,134.49],[134.49,134.65],[134.65,135.11],[135.11,135.27],[135.27,135.5],[135.5,135.97],[136.24,136.47],[136.47,137.25],[137.25,137.56],[137.56,138.18],[138.18,138.41],[138.41,139.27],[139.27,140.04],[140.32,140.7],[140.7,141.4],[141.4,141.56],[141.56,141.95],[142.34,143.04],[143.31,143.85],[143.85,144.01],[144.01,144.32],[144.32,144.55],[144.55,144.71],[144.71,145.02],[145.02,145.79],[146.07,146.61],[146.88,147.27],[147.27,147.5],[147.5,148.28],[148.55,149.02],[149.02,149.17],[149.17,149.56]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Their alumni include Thurgood Marshall, Martin Luther King Jr., Toni Morrison and Kamala Harris.","start":150.52,"end":158.43,"words":[[150.57,150.85],[150.85,151.41],[151.41,151.97],[151.97,152.44],[152.44,153.0],[153.33,153.8],[153.8,154.17],[154.17,154.45],[154.45,155.01],[155.34,155.81],[155.81,156.46],[156.46,156.74],[156.74,157.3],[157.3,157.86]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Debated: you may see the claim that Black women are “the most educated group in America.”","start":158.78,"end":163.79,"words":[[158.83,159.39],[159.61,159.74],[159.74,159.93],[159.93,160.06],[160.06,160.18],[160.18,160.5],[160.5,160.69],[160.69,160.94],[160.94,161.25],[161.25,161.32],[161.32,161.44],[161.44,161.76],[161.76,162.39],[162.39,162.64],[162.64,162.77],[162.77,163.27]]},{"el":"s2","text":"It comes from college enrollment figures.","start":164.14,"end":166.85,"words":[[164.18,164.32],[164.32,164.58],[164.58,164.85],[164.85,165.25],[165.25,165.91],[165.91,166.31]]},{"el":"s2","text":"By degrees completed, other groups are higher.","start":167.2,"end":170.48,"words":[[167.24,167.46],[167.46,167.9],[167.9,168.64],[168.9,169.13],[169.13,169.5],[169.5,169.57],[169.57,169.94]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The accurate version is still powerful: Black women pursue higher education at very high rates while facing some of the largest pay gaps.","start":170.83,"end":180.0,"words":[[170.87,171.04],[171.04,171.61],[171.61,172.02],[172.02,172.19],[172.19,172.51],[172.51,173.17],[173.46,173.79],[173.79,174.2],[174.2,174.61],[174.61,174.94],[174.94,175.76],[175.76,175.92],[175.92,176.25],[176.25,176.49],[176.49,176.91],[176.91,177.23],[177.23,177.73],[177.73,177.97],[177.97,178.14],[178.14,178.3],[178.3,178.88],[178.88,179.12],[179.12,179.53]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Achievement against every barrier","start":180.9,"end":183.3,"words":[[180.95,181.71],[181.71,182.22],[182.22,182.55],[182.55,183.06]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In 1858 the U.S. Attorney General ruled that enslaved inventors could not hold patents.","start":184.0,"end":191.86,"words":[[184.05,184.22],[184.22,185.42],[185.42,185.59],[185.59,186.02],[186.45,186.88],[186.88,187.56],[187.56,187.91],[187.91,188.16],[188.16,188.85],[188.85,189.53],[189.53,189.79],[189.79,190.05],[190.05,190.48],[190.48,191.25]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Free Black inventors patented anyway.","start":192.21,"end":194.93,"words":[[192.23,192.44],[192.44,192.72],[192.72,193.27],[193.27,193.9],[193.9,194.39]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Economist Lisa Cook (now a Federal Reserve governor) showed in 2014 that Black patenting rose after the Civil War and then fell sharply as lynchings, riots and segregation laws spread, with a steep drop after the Tulsa massacre.","start":195.28,"end":211.52,"words":[[195.33,196.1],[196.1,196.43],[196.43,196.69],[196.69,196.94],[196.94,197.11],[197.11,197.7],[197.7,198.13],[198.13,198.63],[198.93,199.27],[199.27,199.44],[199.44,200.37],[200.37,200.62],[200.62,200.96],[200.96,201.72],[201.72,202.06],[202.06,202.4],[202.4,202.57],[202.57,202.99],[202.99,203.16],[203.16,203.41],[203.41,203.67],[203.67,203.92],[203.92,204.35],[204.35,204.51],[204.51,205.28],[205.57,206.08],[206.08,206.33],[206.33,207.26],[207.26,207.52],[207.52,208.03],[208.32,208.58],[208.58,208.75],[208.75,209.08],[209.08,209.42],[209.42,209.76],[209.76,209.93],[209.93,210.35],[210.35,210.95]]},{"el":"s3","text":"The innovation was there.","start":211.87,"end":213.63,"words":[[211.93,212.06],[212.06,212.66],[212.66,212.85],[212.85,213.12]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Violence suppressed it.","start":213.98,"end":215.7,"words":[[214.03,214.54],[214.54,214.99],[214.99,215.19]]},{"el":"s3","text":"A few of the people who succeeded anyway: Garrett Morgan (an improved traffic signal and a safety hood), Madam C.J. Walker (one of the first American women to become a self-made millionaire), Dr. Charles Drew (large-scale blood banks), and Katherine Johnson (orbital calculations for NASA).","start":216.05,"end":234.98,"words":[[216.09,216.24],[216.24,216.47],[216.47,216.62],[216.62,216.77],[216.77,217.15],[217.15,217.3],[217.3,217.91],[217.91,218.44],[218.7,219.08],[219.08,219.46],[219.46,219.61],[219.61,220.14],[220.14,220.6],[220.6,221.05],[221.05,221.28],[221.28,221.43],[221.43,221.89],[221.89,222.19],[222.45,222.83],[222.83,223.36],[223.74,224.05],[224.05,224.27],[224.27,224.42],[224.42,224.58],[224.58,224.88],[224.88,225.48],[225.48,225.86],[225.86,226.02],[226.02,226.39],[226.39,226.55],[226.55,227.15],[227.15,227.83],[228.1,228.55],[228.93,229.31],[229.31,229.54],[229.54,230.22],[230.22,230.52],[230.52,230.98],[231.24,231.47],[231.47,231.93],[231.93,232.46],[232.46,232.91],[232.91,233.9],[233.9,234.05],[234.05,234.43]]},{"el":"h4","text":"The myth of innate inferiority","start":235.88,"end":238.02,"words":[[235.93,236.08],[236.08,236.31],[236.31,236.46],[236.46,236.91],[236.91,237.88]]},{"el":"s4","text":"The claim that racial gaps reflect inborn differences in ability is old.","start":238.72,"end":243.54,"words":[[238.77,238.92],[238.92,239.29],[239.29,239.51],[239.51,239.95],[239.95,240.25],[240.25,240.76],[240.76,241.13],[241.13,241.8],[241.8,241.95],[241.95,242.46],[242.46,242.61],[242.61,242.98]]},{"el":"s4","text":"It was the core of the scientific racism in the module on science.","start":243.89,"end":248.39,"words":[[243.94,244.09],[244.09,244.32],[244.32,244.48],[244.48,244.63],[244.63,244.79],[244.79,244.94],[244.94,245.72],[245.72,246.33],[246.33,246.49],[246.49,246.64],[246.64,247.11],[247.11,247.26],[247.26,247.8]]},{"el":"s4","text":"In 1996 the American Psychological Association's task force on intelligence found no direct evidence supporting a genetic explanation for the Black-white difference in test scores.","start":248.74,"end":260.48,"words":[[248.79,248.94],[248.94,250.15],[250.15,250.29],[250.29,250.87],[250.87,251.79],[251.79,252.72],[252.72,253.01],[253.01,253.22],[253.22,253.37],[253.37,254.15],[254.15,254.51],[254.51,254.72],[254.72,255.22],[255.22,255.72],[255.72,256.22],[256.22,256.37],[256.37,256.94],[256.94,257.8],[257.8,257.94],[257.94,258.08],[258.08,258.65],[258.65,259.15],[259.15,259.3],[259.3,259.58],[259.58,259.94]]},{"el":"s4","text":"The gap on the National Assessment of Educational Progress narrowed considerably from the 1970s to the late 1980s, far too fast for genes, as schools desegregated and resources reached Black students.","start":260.83,"end":274.48,"words":[[260.88,261.03],[261.03,261.25],[261.25,261.39],[261.39,261.54],[261.54,262.05],[262.05,262.64],[262.64,262.78],[262.78,263.66],[263.66,264.25],[264.25,264.69],[264.69,265.56],[265.56,265.86],[265.86,266.0],[266.0,267.1],[267.1,267.25],[267.25,267.39],[267.39,267.69],[267.69,268.64],[268.89,269.04],[269.04,269.19],[269.19,269.48],[269.48,269.62],[269.62,270.06],[270.32,270.47],[270.47,270.83],[270.83,271.78],[271.78,272.0],[272.0,272.51],[272.51,272.88],[272.88,273.17],[273.17,273.9]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Average test scores in every group have risen over generations, which shows how much environment matters.","start":274.83,"end":282.45,"words":[[274.86,275.35],[275.35,275.68],[275.68,276.0],[276.0,276.17],[276.17,276.49],[276.49,276.82],[276.82,277.06],[277.06,277.47],[277.47,277.8],[277.8,278.86],[279.14,279.47],[279.47,279.79],[279.79,280.04],[280.04,280.36],[280.36,281.34],[281.34,281.83]]},{"el":"h5","text":"What allies can do with this","start":283.35,"end":285.58,"words":[[283.39,283.71],[283.71,284.23],[284.23,284.55],[284.55,284.76],[284.76,285.07],[285.07,285.39]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Hiring bias is one of the few forms of discrimination that ordinary employees can fix from inside.","start":286.28,"end":292.78,"words":[[286.32,286.84],[286.84,287.21],[287.21,287.36],[287.36,287.58],[287.58,287.73],[287.73,287.87],[287.87,288.1],[288.1,288.39],[288.39,288.54],[288.54,289.58],[289.58,289.8],[289.8,290.32],[290.32,290.91],[290.91,291.13],[291.13,291.43],[291.43,291.73],[291.73,292.24]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Blind résumé review, structured interviews with the same questions for every candidate, “fair chance” policies that delay questions about criminal records, and regular audits of who gets interviewed all reduce it.","start":293.13,"end":306.8,"words":[[293.18,293.63],[293.63,294.16],[294.16,294.61],[294.87,295.55],[295.55,296.15],[296.15,296.38],[296.38,296.53],[296.53,296.83],[296.83,297.51],[297.51,297.66],[297.66,297.96],[297.96,298.71],[298.97,299.2],[299.2,299.57],[299.57,300.1],[300.1,300.33],[300.33,300.7],[300.7,301.38],[301.38,301.75],[301.75,302.36],[302.36,302.88],[303.15,303.37],[303.37,303.9],[303.9,304.27],[304.27,304.42],[304.42,304.57],[304.57,304.88],[304.88,305.48],[305.48,305.63],[305.63,306.08],[306.08,306.3]]},{"el":"s5","text":"The quest for this module asks you to propose one at your workplace.","start":307.15,"end":311.23,"words":[[307.19,307.33],[307.33,307.69],[307.69,307.83],[307.83,308.04],[308.04,308.47],[308.47,308.76],[308.76,308.9],[308.9,309.04],[309.04,309.54],[309.54,309.75],[309.75,309.9],[309.9,310.04],[310.04,310.68]]}]}